<newsitem itemid="158240" id="root" date="1996-10-31" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Body Shop H1 profits rise 30 percent.</title>
<headline>Body Shop H1 profits rise 30 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.6		    vs 2.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.5		    vs 1.08</p>
<p> Pretax		     11.8		   vs 9.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   117.1		  vs 105.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Body Shop International Plc is a health and beauty product retailer, with worldwide franchises. The group's chairman Gordon Roddick said the results were in line with forecasts. He added that sales in the first month of the second half were flat on a like-for-like basis.</p>
<p> Retail sales	     275.5		  vs 243.4</p>
<p> Operating results	12.0		   vs 9.5</p>
<p> Interest		   0.2		    vs 0.4</p>
<p> Tax			  4.8		    vs 3.7</p>
<p> Attributable	     7.0		    vs 5.4</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 9</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 19</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
